# =============================================================================
# Burst trie / B-trie "burst" event (Askitis & Zobel).
# A container (bucket) accumulates strings cheaply. When its occupancy crosses
# the burst threshold it BURSTS: a trie node is created, and the bucket's
# strings are redistributed into smaller child buckets keyed by their (now
# consumed) leading character. The leading byte moves into the trie edge, so the
# child buckets store the suffixes only.
#
# Color key (rendered by the wrapper):
#   amber = bucket / container storage   ·   blue = the new trie (index) node
# =============================================================================

  BEFORE  —  one bucket, near the burst threshold

  +-------------------------------+
  | bucket  (threshold: 4)        |
  |-------------------------------|
  |  "car"   "cat"   "cup"  "cab" |   <- 4th insert crosses the threshold
  +-------------------------------+
                |
              BURST


  AFTER  —  bucket replaced by a trie node + smaller child buckets

                +-----------------+
                |   trie node     |
                |  'a'        'u' |
                +-----------------+
                  /             \
            'a'  /               \  'u'
                v                 v
     +--------------------+   +-----------+
     | bucket (a*)        |   | bucket(u*)|
     |--------------------|   |-----------|
     |  "r"   "t"   "b"   |   |  "p"      |
     | (was car/cat/cab,  |   | (was cup, |
     |  lead 'c','a' gone)|   |  lead 'c' |
     +--------------------+   |  'u' gone)|
                             +-----------+

  Leading bytes 'c' then 'a'/'u' are now encoded by the path to each bucket,
  so child buckets hold only suffixes => more strings per page, fewer compares.
